# Generated script output - never commit these.
#
# The scripts in this repository are read-only diagnostics, but most of them
# export their findings. That output contains real data from whichever tenant or
# device the script was run against: device names, serial numbers, user names,
# installed app inventory, compliance state and organisation-scale totals.
#
# Even when device and user names are masked, the software inventory and the
# scale of the numbers still identify the organisation. This repository is
# public, so generated output must stay local.
#
# Several scripts write into their own folder inside this working tree, so a
# plain `git add .` would stage real data without any warning. For example:
#   Get-FleetServicingChannelReport.ps1 -ExportCsv
#     -> FleetServicingChannel-<timestamp>.csv, via Join-Path $PSScriptRoot
#
# To commit a deliberately sanitised example that one of these patterns blocks,
# override per file with:  git add -f <path>

# Report output folders
reports/
Reports/

# CSV exports - most scripts take -ExportCsv or -OutputPath and default to
# a .csv in the current directory or alongside the script
*.csv

# JSON payloads built from the local device's real app inventory
# (Export-StartMenuPinConfig.ps1 defaults to .\ConfigureStartPins.json)
ConfigureStartPins.json

# Rendered HTML reports produced alongside the CSVs
latest-*.html
*-analysis.html
*-report.html

# Local scratch
*.log
*.tmp
